WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.069
In 1911, a wave of revolution swept across China.

00:00:04.069 --> 00:00:08.838
The Qing dynasty ended in 1912, and the imperial system passed into history.

00:00:08.838 --> 00:00:11.998
People cut off their queues to welcome a new era.

00:00:11.998 --> 00:00:15.702
The system of emperors, over 2,000 years old, came to an end.

00:00:15.702 --> 00:00:19.251
In the 20th century, China and Taiwan went through many changes.

00:00:19.251 --> 00:00:23.050
The great wheel of the times kept turning forward.

00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:27.607
War and political change transformed countless families.

00:00:27.617 --> 00:00:31.943
Many people left their hometowns to live in new places.

00:00:31.943 --> 00:00:35.145
Later the economy gradually grew, and cities became more prosperous.

00:00:35.145 --> 00:00:38.058
Tall buildings and ports changed people's lives.

00:00:38.058 --> 00:00:41.555
Trains and ships connected distant cities.

00:00:41.555 --> 00:00:45.523
Today, the Chinese-speaking world spans the globe.

00:00:45.523 --> 00:00:49.711
Mainland China, Taiwan, and Hong Kong each have different stories.

00:00:49.711 --> 00:00:53.910
Usage and writing habits are not entirely the same in each place.

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:58.730
Singapore and overseas Chinese communities also speak Chinese.

00:00:58.730 --> 00:01:01.458
Studying history helps us understand these differences.
